{"message":"Thank you for coming. NP took the largest share of the vote and the largest bloc in this chamber, so I think it's reasonable that a government be built around that fact — with me as head of government. I'm not interested in dragging this out through a second election if we can avoid it, and I suspect neither are you, but I'm equally not interested in a platform that our voters won't recognise as ours.

Here's my opening position: any government I lead needs a credible economic platform — firmly market-oriented, not the muddled centre — and a serious law and order stance, tough on crime, not another round of rehabilitation rhetoric. I'll also want a binding cap on spending growth written into the programme; that's non-negotiable for me sitting in cabinet. Beyond that I'm genuinely flexible — on environment, immigration, social policy, transport, there's room to find language that lets both our bases live with the result.

So tell me plainly: where does FF actually sit on economic policy and on crime, and what do you need from me to bring your people into a government rather than sit outside sniping at one? I'd rather build something solid with you than spend months finding out the hard way that we can't.","ending":"continue"}
